{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-9v:000001:issue_created:sase-9v","timestamp":"2026-07-26T15:32:00Z","actor":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-9v","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-9v","title":"Harden the bead subsystem against the verified gaps from the post-sase-9r/9s review","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-07-26T15:32:00Z","created_by":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","updated_at":"2026-07-26T15:32:00Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"The verified bugs and inconsistencies from the five-reviewer bead-subsystem audit are fixed: every runner bead mutation runs under the store write lock, retained claims are always committed and publishable, claim residue is reconciled and visible to doctor, git probe failures fail closed, the managed sync worker clears cooldowns and stops leaking process state, the bead_store_refresh chop fits its own time budget, the `sase bead work` CLI honors its confirmation/JSON/reporting contracts, legacy epic approvals stop blocking the ACE event loop, sase-core bead mutations are atomic against each other, dead code left by the recent refactors is removed, and docs/beads.md matches current behavior.","notes":"","design":"sase/repos/plans/202607/bead_review_hardening.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
